{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And He said, “Is it good”</b> — like: ואכות אותו טחון היטב, and the grinding is a complete, finished grinding." "And the meaning: why does it burn you so — and Yefet said: “Does it burn you that I do good to whomever I wish.” And this is folly:"], :book :jonah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "The Hebrew quotes a form אכות (root כות/כתת, 'to beat/crush') in a parallel usage of היטב; the phrase appears to be a technical or dialectal illustration whose exact provenance is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Jonah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=19&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:07:15.640813199Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}